{
  "tema": 5109,
  "slug": "trabaje-preterito-ar",
  "titulo": "Regular -ar verbs in the preterite",
  "subtitulo": "Ayer trabajé y Beto descansó.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "To form the preterite of a regular -ar verb, drop -ar and add -é, -aste, -ó, -amos, -aron. The accents on -é and -ó are essential: hablo is I speak, habló is he spoke.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The preterite tells what happened and finished: **ayer**, **anoche**, **el sábado**, **la semana pasada**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "habl-",
            "+",
            "-é / -aste / -ó / -amos / -aron"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Ending",
            "hablar",
            "surfear"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "**-é**",
              "hablé",
              "surfeé"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "**-aste**",
              "hablaste",
              "surfeaste"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "**-ó**",
              "habló",
              "surfeó"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "**-amos**",
              "hablamos",
              "surfeamos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos, ustedes",
              "**-aron**",
              "hablaron",
              "surfearon"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The accent changes the meaning: **hablo** (_I speak_) vs **habló** (_he spoke_); **hable** vs **hablé** (_I spoke_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Nosotros** is the same as the present: **hablamos** = _we speak_ or _we spoke_. Context (**ayer**, **el año pasado**) tells you which."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Stem changes from the present disappear: **pensar** → **pensé**, **contar** → **conté**, **jugar** → **jugué**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Spelling in **yo** only: **-car → qué** (busqué), **-gar → gué** (llegué), **-zar → cé** (empecé)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the **ó** is a finish line. Once you cross it, the action is over."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ayer ==trabajé== diez horas en el taller.",
              "en": "Yesterday I worked ten hours at the shop."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Hablaste== con tu jefe?",
              "en": "Did you talk to your boss?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi hermano ==compró== una tabla nueva en Rosarito.",
              "en": "My brother bought a new board in Rosarito."
            },
            {
              "es": "El sábado ==entrenamos== dos horas.",
              "en": "On Saturday we trained for two hours."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mis vecinos ==plantaron== cilantro en el patio.",
              "en": "My neighbors planted cilantro in the yard."
            },
            {
              "es": "Anoche ==miré== tres capítulos de _The Expanse_.",
              "en": "Last night I watched three episodes of The Expanse."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿A qué hora ==llegaron== ustedes?",
              "en": "What time did you guys arrive?"
            },
            {
              "es": "La clase ==terminó== tarde.",
              "en": "Class ended late."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
